# dis/-rooted build context. Mirrors the monorepo-root /.dockerignore.
#
# Docker resolves .dockerignore at the CONTEXT ROOT, so this file — and only this
# file — bounds the context for every image whose context is `dis/`:
#
#   dis/terraform/docker/csv-ingest-worker.Dockerfile
#     docker build -f terraform/docker/csv-ingest-worker.Dockerfile -t csv-ingest-worker .
#   dis/terraform/docker/streaming-consumer.Dockerfile
#     docker build -f terraform/docker/streaming-consumer.Dockerfile -t streaming-consumer .
#   dis/infra/local/fakes.Dockerfile
#     docker compose build (docker-compose.yml, `context: .`) — the local
#     customer-master and identity-service fakes
#
# NOT covered here, verified rather than assumed:
#   - dis/terraform/docker/dis-ui-ver2.Dockerfile builds with `services/dis-ui-ver2`
#     as its context (stated in its header AND passed as the final `build` arg in
#     terraform/docker/cloudbuild-dis-ui-ver2.yaml), so its context root is that
#     directory, not dis/. This file is never read for it.
#   - The three monorepo-root-context images (dis-ui-server, thalamus-square,
#     thalamus-clover) read /.dockerignore instead.
#
# --- weight: never a COPY source ---------------------------------------------------
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.terraform/

# --- dev-only content that WOULD otherwise land in a shipped image -----------------
# The worker Dockerfiles copy whole package directories (`COPY libs libs`,
# `COPY services/<name> services/<name>`), so every tests/ directory under them rode
# along until this file existed.
#
# Verified safe for all three dis/-rooted builds:
#   - All 15 hatch wheel targets under libs/ and services/ are `packages =
#     ["src/<pkg>"]`; a wheel build never reaches outside src/. The root dis project
#     is `[tool.uv] package = false`, so it is not built at all.
#   - No COPY in any of the three Dockerfiles names a tests/ or scripts/ path.
#   - No module under any src/ tree imports from tests/ or scripts/.
#   - dis-testing is a LIB: the fakes the compose stack runs are
#     src/dis_testing/fakes/{customer_master,identity_service}.py, under src/ and NOT
#     under tests/, so `make run-local` is unaffected. Proven by bringing the stack up.
**/tests/
**/scripts/
**/.env
**/.env.*
